.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_011_batch_commands.md:17:Not implemented. F-010 action loading/running is also not implemented yet. The Electron app currently exposes only local Git/data bridge methods, watches markdown changes under the project root and has no script-folder config, script discovery, command runner, parameter model or action-change notification channel.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_011_batch_commands.md:20:- Extend the F-010 action model with generated `command` actions sourced from configured script folders. Every generated action has a stable `id` that does not depend on its editable name.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_011_batch_commands.md:21:- Support project-level script folders and Electron-app-level script folders; require Electron/local mode for execution.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_011_batch_commands.md:23:- Resolve parameter values and placeholders at run time from the selected action context, matching F-010 placeholder behavior.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_011_batch_commands.md:25:- Watch configured folders, debounce reloads and publish action-list updates to React when scripts or sidecar json files are added, changed or removed.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_011_batch_commands.md:26:- Fail fast with clear load/run errors for invalid sidecar json, duplicate generated action names, unsupported extensions, missing configured folders, missing bash executable or attempts to run outside the configured folders.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_011_batch_commands.md:30:- Opening a local Electron project loads script actions from configured project and Electron script folders.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_011_batch_commands.md:32:- Running `.bat`, `.cmd`, `.ps1` and configured `.sh` scripts executes through Electron with placeholders and configured parameters resolved.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\B_064_unified_action_runner_lifecycle_and_isolation_defects.md:17:- `ActionRunnerService` stores the active project and actions folder on the singleton. An execution snapshots its action graph and context, but later phases read `this.project` and `this.actionsFolder`. Opening another project or switching branch during a run can execute a later phase or append history in the new project.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\B_064_unified_action_runner_lifecycle_and_isolation_defects.md:20:- Root `extraPrompt` is passed to every linked agent prompt and command placeholder. Agent, model, and thinking-level overrides are correctly root-only; prompt input must follow the same ownership rule.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\B_064_unified_action_runner_lifecycle_and_isolation_defects.md:30:- Snapshot project and actions-folder references in each execution and use that snapshot for every phase and history write. Project changes must not retarget an active execution.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\B_064_unified_action_runner_lifecycle_and_isolation_defects.md:63:- Every execution uses the project and actions folder captured at start for all phases and history writes.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_009_affects_editor.md:20:- Add a repository file listing path to the storage contract and Electron bridge so GitHub and local projects can provide normalized repo-relative paths, not only markdown files from the working folder.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_013_desktop_app.md:17:Electron already opens the React app in a `BrowserWindow`, loads the configured app URL, disables context isolation, and exposes a preload bridge as `window.md2Data`. The local Git path supports opening a `.git` folder, loading markdown files, creating the working folder, switching branches, committing, pushing and watching markdown changes. React detects the Electron bridge and can open a local project through `ProjectWorkspace`.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_013_desktop_app.md:30:- Surface failures from folder selection, Git commands, file watching, WebSocket startup and agent execution as user-visible errors.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_017_search.md:14:Add an easy-to-access text search (with optional RegExp mode and agent-built expressions) over cards, history and other special folders, with grouped results and navigation to the matching card or file, integrated into the borderless window's drag bar area.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_017_search.md:19:The parsed project data is available through `useProjectState()`, which returns the `DataService` state including a `ProjectSnapshot` with `activeCards`, `backgroundCards` and `workingFolder`. `markdownParsingService.splitCards` already splits files into active vs background using `isRootWorkingFolderFile` (root markdown files under the working folder are active; everything in subfolders is background), and produces `ProjectCard` objects with `content` (body only), a parsed `header` (`CardHeader`: id, title, status, owner, affects, policy, etc.), `isActive` and `path`. A search module can consume this snapshot directly; frontmatter parsing already lives in `markdown_parsing_service.ts` and must not be duplicated. Background results are not currently grouped by their first subfolder anywhere.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_017_search.md:29:- Search active root cards by full body content and header fields by default. Search background cards from subfolders by header fields by default, with an option to include full body content. Use `ProjectCard` data produced by the shared parsing service; the search module must not parse frontmatter itself.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_017_search.md:31:- Group results with active cards first, then background results grouped by first folder under the working folder, such as `history` or `architecture`.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_017_search.md:40:- Active cards are searched by full content and appear before background/special-folder results.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_017_search.md:41:- Background cards from history, architecture and other subfolders are searchable by header fields; enabling full search includes their body content.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_017_search.md:43:- Results are grouped by active cards and by special folder name, with enough context to identify the match.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_016_config.md:21:Project config is a small in-memory object. `createProjectConfig(pushMode)` builds it from hard-coded/default values: working folder `design`, default card types, default card body template and the selected push mode. `ProjectWorkspace` owns the push-mode select, recreates config when opening a GitHub or local project, and reads card types/working folder back from `DataService`. `use_app_bootstrap.ts` restores the last project with auto push mode. No project config file is loaded, merged, validated or saved.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_016_config.md:44:- Opening a project loads project config, merges it over defaults, and uses it for working folder, push mode and card type settings.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_015_remarkable_integration.md:19:- Store import metadata in a project-local json file under the working folder so the UI can mark files as new, changed or already imported.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_015_remarkable_integration.md:32:- Imported image files are stored in the same folder as the target card and referenced from that card with relative markdown links.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:14:Replace the free-text owner/repo/branch fields with real selection flows: pick a repository from the authenticated user's repositories, pick/switch a branch from an actual branch list ("allow switch branch from menu"), and ask the user which folder to use when the configured working folder is missing.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:17:`ProjectWorkspace` opens GitHub projects from three plain `TextField`s (owner, repository, branch) and switches branches by typing a name. `listBranches` is fully implemented in `GithubStorageService`, `LocalGitStorageService` and the Electron bridge but has **no UI consumer**. `GithubStorageService.findRepository` exists but is also unused. When the configured working folder does not exist, `createProject`/`loadProject` silently create it with a README instead of asking the user which folder to use (`data management.md`).
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:21:- After choosing a repository (or local folder), populate a branch dropdown from `listBranches` and preselect the default/current branch; branch switching uses the same dropdown, not free text.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:23:- Working-folder resolution on open: if the configured folder is missing, show a chooser listing the repo's top-level folders with options "use folder X", "create '{configured}' from template". Only create the template after explicit confirmation.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:24:- Persist the chosen working folder into the project config (`md2.config.json`) so the question is asked once per project.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:30:- When the working folder is missing, the user is asked to pick an existing folder or create the configured one from the template; nothing is created without confirmation.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:31:- The chosen working folder is stored in project config and reused on the next open.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_027_repository_branch_selection.md:33:- Tests cover repository listing/filtering, branch dropdown population, the missing-folder chooser and config persistence.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_030_action_entry_point_display.md:17:`ActionEntryPoints` (`app/src/components/actions/action_entry_points.tsx`) renders every card action as a generic Play icon and every file/folder action through a DotsVertical overflow menu. The `icon` field is parsed and validated by the action loader (`action_definition_loader.ts`) but never used by any component. Cards have no context menu at all — the design lists "small icon buttons, in context menu, menu items" for cards.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_025_card_deletion.md:24:- Deleting a card with agent log references leaves the log files in place (they live outside the working folder) but the references disappear with the card.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_026_external_change_watching.md:28:- Creating a markdown file in the working folder outside the app makes it appear as a card (status `new` when no header) without reopening the project.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_010_actions.md:17:> - [[F-010c]] Electron action execution and chaining - Electron runner, placeholders, `onBefore`/main/`on`/`onAfter`, logs and status
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_010_actions.md:19:> - [[F-010e]] state triggers and folder watching - `onState`, card current-action state and hot reload
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_010_actions.md:25:Load ID-based JSON action definitions from the project's actions folder, show context-sensitive action entry points, and execute actions only through an Electron-side action runner. Support agent and command actions, the built-in custom-prompt action, placeholders, `onBefore`/`on`/`onAfter` chaining, `onState`, `needsWorkTree`, cancellation, and `appliesTo`.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_010_actions.md:39:- Show compact entry points near matching cards, files, and folders based on `appliesTo`.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_010_actions.md:42:- The renderer sends only `{ actionId, context, runInput }`. Electron reloads and validates the persisted definition by `id`, resolves placeholders, and executes the complete chain.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_010_actions.md:49:- Watch the actions folder in local Electron mode and publish validated definition changes to React.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_021_parsing_service.md:29:  - active/background card splitting for a working folder;
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_024_history_archiving.md:14:Implement the "complete release" operation from F-003: move the current active (root working-folder) cards into a new `history/{release}` subfolder and commit the moves, so the board is cleared for the next release while archived cards stay searchable.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_024_history_archiving.md:17:The `history` folder is recognized for tree display (`DEFAULT_SPECIAL_FOLDERS` in `app/src/data/file_tree.ts`) and search grouping, and id numbering already scans subfolders, but no code moves cards. There is no release UI, no storage-level move/rename operation (`StorageService` has no delete or move), and no commit path for relocating files.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_024_history_archiving.md:21:- Add `DataService.completeRelease(releaseName)`: flush pending commits, move every active card file to `{workingFolder}/history/{releaseName}/`, commit as a single logical change and push per push mode, then reload/refresh the snapshot so the moved cards become background cards.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_024_history_archiving.md:25:- Id generation must keep considering archived files so ids stay unique (already the case via subfolder scanning; add a regression test).
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_024_history_archiving.md:29:- After completion the card board is empty and the archived cards appear under the history folder in the tree and in background search results.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_024_history_archiving.md:36:- `design\feature_descriptions\F_003_special_folders.md`
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_033_agent_and_model_selection.md:22:- Model the agent as a named profile: `{ name, command, modelArgument?, models?: string[], defaultModel? }`. Ship built-in profiles (codex, claude, system default) and allow user-defined profiles with a free-form command template supporting a `{{model}}` placeholder.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_047_running_actions_and_agents.md:38:- Add Electron unit tests for id lookup, request validation, placeholders, every chain phase, output matching, failure results, events, history, and cancellation during command and agent phases.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_049_agent_chat_fab_popup.md:62:   suppress it entirely when there are no previous runs, instead of rendering the "No previous runs" placeholder
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_050_one_shot_agent_conversations.md:62:- When switching back to a provider with an older valid session, resume that session and include all transcript messages added since its synchronization cursor. Advance the cursor only after successful completion.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_050_one_shot_agent_conversations.md:69:- Conversations without any provider id, including older logs, use the same full-history start path.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_053_card_number_from_header_id.md:30:- Numbering stays per-prefix / per-card-type and continues to scan the whole project including subfolders and archived history cards.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_053_card_number_from_header_id.md:44:- Per-type independence, subfolder/history inclusion, and the configured separator behavior are preserved.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_052_agent_popup_conversation_layout_and_expansion.md:30:- Place a divider below the chat log and the prompt input below the divider. Empty/new conversations show an empty chat area without an inline run-history placeholder.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_055_agent_file_change_tracking.md:95:- **Path outside the working folder / project root.** Rejected by the root-confinement guard and
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_054_agent_token_usage_tracking.md:36:  - **per version (release)** — sum usage across the cards in each `history/{release}/` folder (see F_024) plus the current active board as the in-progress version;
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_054_agent_token_usage_tracking.md:43:- A provider event without a usage object (older CLI, cancelled/failed turn): contributes 0, never `NaN`.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:49:- action history is split into path-derived, per-action files under the ignored `logs` folder — unstable identity (collides after moves/normalization) and stored per-worktree instead of one project-owned location;
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:62:- card activity: `<projectFolder>/activity/card__<cardInternalId>.json`;
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:63:- project-origin activity: `<projectFolder>/activity/project.json` (no card id).
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:110:- All records persist; no exact UI cap required — a reasonable display limit (e.g. 50) may be applied for performance, with older entries stated as hidden. Paging not required.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:154:- Two collaborators edit the same tracked activity file on different branches: normal Git conflict handling applies.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_060_card_commit_diff_viewer.md:158:- Activity stored once per card under tracked `<projectFolder>/activity`, keyed by `cardInternalId`, written in the primary checkout regardless of execution worktree.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_057_edit_prepared_action_prompt.md:31:The action popup starts with an empty `extraPrompt` field. On `Run`, React sends the selected action id, context, run-time agent settings, and `extraPrompt` to Electron. Electron reloads the canonical action, resolves context placeholders, substitutes `{{card-prompt}}` or appends the extra text, optionally adds the tracked-file instruction, and sends the resulting prompt to the agent.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_057_edit_prepared_action_prompt.md:38:- Electron reloads the canonical action definition by id, resolves the same execution project or assigned worktree used by the action runner, resolves all prompt placeholders, and applies every prompt addition that would otherwise be applied immediately before starting the root agent action.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\F_057_edit_prepared_action_prompt.md:83:- Tests cover exact prompt preview/execution parity, placeholder and worktree resolution, tracked-file instruction handling, empty-string presence, action/context selection races, preservation of user edits, preparation errors, custom prompt, phrases, linked actions, and local/remote bridge exposure.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_006_split_local_git_service.md:20:- `desktop/project_files.js` — load project/root/config, read/write/delete/move files, working-folder template, watchProject.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_004_split_project_toolbar_menu_dialogs.md:21:  - `working_folder_chooser_dialog.tsx` — missing-working-folder chooser flow.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_001_initialize.md:14:Create all folders and sub projects (React app, Electron app), install packages by running the install commands so we get the latest versions of everything. Result is a runnable skeleton app (React app starts, Electron app hosts it) that all features build on.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_001_initialize.md:20:Two independent, standalone sub-projects in two plain folders at the repo root, each with its own `package.json` (no monorepo / workspaces):
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_001_initialize.md:36:- `app/` and `desktop/` exist as two standalone folders, each with its own `package.json` and lockfile.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_012_unify_react_electron_validators.md:23:1. **Shared module (preferred)**: create a dependency-free shared package/folder (e.g. `shared/` with plain `.js` + `.d.ts`, or a TS source compiled to CJS in the desktop build step) containing the validation/normalization logic; both `app` and `desktop` import it. The desktop currently has no build step, so plain JS with type declarations consumed by the app is the low-friction option.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_019_unify_open_document_drafts_and_save_state.md:84:5. A failed commit leaves it dirty. Completion of an older revision cannot clear newer edits.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_019_unify_open_document_drafts_and_save_state.md:120:- Successful physical batch persistence clears only the saved revision; failures and newer edits remain dirty.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_008_split_action_runner_helpers.md:19:- Move placeholder and agent-prompt resolution to Electron; only Electron reads persisted `prompt` and `command`.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_008_split_action_runner_helpers.md:27:- React contains no action-chain runner, placeholder resolver, executable prompt builder, or output-matching implementation.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_008_split_action_runner_helpers.md:29:- Electron helpers are unit-tested for IDs, placeholders, phases, output matching, statuses and cancellation.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_017_markdown_editor_data_sources.md:228:Presentation props unchanged: `flushOnBlur`, `stickyToolbar`, `hideToolbar`, `readOnly`, `overlayContainer`, `placeholders`, `toolbarContents`.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_013_action_runner_dependency_surface.md:23:  - action environment: project, actions folder, supported agent configuration and worktree preparation.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_015_split_github_storage_service.md:17:Follow the established collaborator pattern (see J-005/J-006): keep `githubStorageService` as the thin facade implementing the storage interface, and extract internal collaborators in the same folder, e.g.:
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:21:This report describes the current working-tree implementation as inspected on 2026-07-15. Continuation handling is actively evolving around provider sessions and transcript synchronization; the refactor must preserve that current behavior rather than reintroduce the older `nativeSessionId`/synthetic-prompt path.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:43:| `desktop/src/shell/local_bridge_dispatch.js` | `start`, `cancel`, `subscribe`, `requireActionsFolder` | Keep bridge method names, request/result shapes, synchronous subscription behavior, and history-folder lookup unchanged. |
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:63:`ActionRunnerService` owns the current project/actions-folder lifecycle, listener set, active execution map, completed-result map, execution-id generation, and start/wait/cancel behavior. This is the correct responsibility for the public facade.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:67:Each start snapshots `project`, `actionsFolder`, `context`, `rootAction`, and `runInput`, then adds an `AbortController`, active agent run id, execution id, and completion promise. The service passes this record through nearly every internal method. That parameter threading is the clearest extraction boundary: the record should become an `ActionExecution` instance.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:86:The module validates the Git root, starts a shell process, buffers stdout/stderr while streaming chunks, maps cancellation, resolves placeholders, enters the worktree lock, and appends history. The actual command path is small and does not justify a service class with no state.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:116:Request/context/run-input validation and placeholder/prompt resolution are pure functions. They do not depend on service state and obscure the class lifecycle at the top of the current file.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:126:- project/actions-folder lifecycle;
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:130:- `start`, `wait`, `cancel`, `subscribe`, `stop`, and `requireActionsFolder`;
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:142:- the immutable start snapshot (`project`, `actionsFolder`, `context`, `rootAction`, `runInput`, `executionId`);
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:176:- command placeholder resolution at execution time.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:188:Move Electron placeholder and prompt resolution here:
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:190:- `resolvePlaceholders`;
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:192:- placeholder patterns.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:217:2. It verifies service readiness and snapshots project/actions folder.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:235:- `context.kind` is one of `card`, `file`, `folder`, or `project`.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:246:- An execution uses the project and actions folder captured at `start` for every linked phase, definition-derived action, conversation load, and history write.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:248:- `stop` cancels every currently registered execution, then clears the current project/actions folder.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:261:- `extraPrompt` replaces `{{card-prompt}}` when the placeholder exists; otherwise nonblank input is appended with two newlines.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:293:- Command and agent history remains keyed by action id, actions folder, and context.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:342:- root project, file, and prompt placeholders;
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:352:- placeholder resolution and root-only prompt input through execution integration.
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:396:- project/actions-folder snapshot across project switches;
.\design\releases\0_0_2\J_016_split_action_runner_service.md:430:- `ActionRunnerService` is a lifecycle/registry facade and contains no chain traversal, command spawning, agent continuation, callback-to-promise adaptation, placeholder implementation, or history-entry construction.

